{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.HorizonFunctor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.HorizonFunctor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HorizonFunctor.ofSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HorizonFunctor.ofSpace","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HorizonFunctor.lean#L63-L76","doc":"**De-axiomatisation (bean `bqfr`): a genuine topological horizon.** Over\nany topological space of configurations with a real degree-0 section `A₀`,\nan aeon is a region and its horizon is the topological **frontier** of the\nregion intersected with the `A₀ = 0` locus. `frontier` is Mathlib's real\nclosure-minus-interior — the genuine \"limits of diagrams in the aeon\"\noperator — so `boundary_nonobservable` is a *theorem* (the boundary lies\nin `{A₀ = 0}` by construction), not an assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HorizonFunctor.boundary_disjoint_observable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HorizonFunctor.boundary_disjoint_observable","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HorizonFunctor.lean#L53-L59","doc":"Restated as set disjointness: `∂(𝒜) ∩ {observable} = ∅`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HorizonFunctor.observable_not_mem_boundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HorizonFunctor.observable_not_mem_boundary","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HorizonFunctor.lean#L47-L51","doc":"The boundary of every aeon is disjoint from the observable subcategory:\nno observable configuration lies on any horizon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HorizonFunctor.boundary_nonobservable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HorizonFunctor.boundary_nonobservable","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HorizonFunctor.lean#L41-L41","doc":"The boundary of an aeon consists of non-observable configurations\n(`A₀|_𝒮 = 0`) — it lands in `Bun ∖ Bun°`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HorizonFunctor.boundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HorizonFunctor.boundary","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HorizonFunctor.lean#L38-L38","doc":"The horizon / boundary map `∂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HorizonFunctor.observable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HorizonFunctor.observable","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HorizonFunctor.lean#L36-L36","doc":"Observability predicate (membership in `Bun°`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HorizonFunctor.Aeon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HorizonFunctor.Aeon","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HorizonFunctor.lean#L34-L34","doc":"Aeons `π₀(Bun°)` (connected components of the observable subcategory). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HorizonFunctor.Config","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HorizonFunctor.Config","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HorizonFunctor.lean#L32-L32","doc":"Objects of the ambient bundle category `Bun(ℙ(V))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HorizonFunctor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HorizonFunctor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HorizonFunctor.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HorizonFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HorizonFunctor","kind":"structure","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/HorizonFunctor.lean#L24-L41","doc":"Data for the horizon functor.\n\nA `definition` carrier: the ambient configurations `Config`, the aeons\n`Aeon = π₀(Bun°)`, the observability predicate, and the boundary map\n`∂`, with the defining property that the boundary lands in the\nnon-observable complement (`A₀ = 0`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:horizon-functor","label":"def:horizon-functor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/horizon-functor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}